  "description": "YURWOZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C112 H132 Eu2 N12 O28 Sm4. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.772-3.872 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.15-107.78°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu2Sm4C112H132N12O28. Article name explicitly identifies Eu(II), Sm(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
